    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0161" n="152" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg152"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/1341: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Greene</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-08-12T17:00:00+01:00">August 12, 1940—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 12—2:41 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>825. Number of passengers sailing on <hi rendition="#italic">American Legion</hi>
                    recorded here follows: Finland 138, Estonia 22, Latvia 18, Lithuania 102, Sweden
                    250, Norway 182, Denmark 84, Germany 88, Netherlands 13, total 897. Of these 16
                    are Latin Americans.</p>
                <p>The capacity of the ship is reported at 905 including temporary cots. The ship’s
                    master requested that a small percentage less than capacity be allowed to permit
                    him latitude in making assignments to the distinguished guest<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d205-f1"/> and party.</p>
                <p>The last group left Stockholm at 1418 today.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Greene</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d205-f1" n="41" xml:id="d205-f1-content">
                <p>Crown Princess of Norway; see <ref target="frus1940v01">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>
                    </ref>, section I under Extension of the European War, entitled “Invasion of
                    Norway and Denmark by Germany.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
